from pathlib import Path
import json,html
from PIL import Image,ImageDraw,ImageFont
O=Path('outputs/30a_final');a=json.loads((O/'audit.json').read_text());font=ImageFont.load_default(size=22)
canvas=Image.new('RGB',(1830,3*930),'#f7f3e8');dr=ImageDraw.Draw(canvas)
for j,(slug,name) in enumerate([('seaside','Seaside'),('rosemary','Rosemary Beach'),('alys','Alys Beach')]):
 y=j*930;dr.text((15,y+4),name+' · 390 px phone / 1440 px desktop',font=font,fill='#34544b');canvas.paste(Image.open(O/f'{slug}-390.png'),(0,y+35));canvas.paste(Image.open(O/f'{slug}-1440.png'),(390,y+30))
canvas.resize((1220,1860)).save(O/'six-views.jpg',quality=92)
rows=''.join(f'<tr><td>{html.escape(r["name"])}</td><td>{r["error_m"]:.3f} m</td><td><a href="{r["source"]}">OSM source</a></td></tr>' for r in a['districts']+a['northSeasideWater'])
photos=''.join(f'<h2>{name}</h2><div class="pair"><a href="{s}-390.png"><img src="{s}-390.png"></a><a href="{s}-1440.png"><img src="{s}-1440.png"></a></div>' for s,name in [('seaside','Seaside'),('rosemary','Rosemary Beach'),('alys','Alys Beach')])
(O/'index.html').write_text('''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>30A · final-detail review</title><style>body{max-width:1500px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 20px;background:#f7f3e8;color:#34544b;font:16px/1.5 system-ui}h1,h2{font-family:Georgia}img{max-width:100%}.pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:390fr 1440fr;gap:18px;align-items:start}table{border-collapse:collapse}td{padding:6px 20px;border-bottom:1px solid #d5d6c5}a{color:#a04b27}.note{background:#fff9e9;padding:20px}</style><h1>30A · final-detail review</h1><p>Installed locally. Approved Region anchors and tap-to-Town flow retained. Phone cards collapse controls to a 42 px bar with a 10 px gap; full-screen canvas. Hard roof planes, ridge lines and standing-seam detail. No console errors observed during the six-view checks.</p><div class="note"><b>Verification limit:</b> All district anchors: 0.000 m against source OSM positions. The 15 water bodies around and north of Seaside: maximum 0.589 m exported boundary error. No checked feature exceeds 150 m. These are same-source fidelity measurements, not independent ground-truth certification.<br><b>Pavilion limitation:</b> Seven added small pavilions are placed at OSM street-end beach-access endpoints. OSM does not separately identify their exact footprints. These remain approximate pavilion placements, not fully verified pavilion centers. Existing central structures are retained. No satellite imagery is shipped in the map.</div><p><a href="audit.json">Full measurements and source links</a> · <a href="pavilion-evidence.json">Pavilion placement evidence</a></p><h2>Region overlay on OSM</h2><img src="region-osm-overlay.png"><h2>Seaside Town overlay on OSM</h2><img src="town-seaside-osm-overlay.png"><h2>Water north of Seaside</h2><img src="north-seaside-water-osm-overlay.png"><p>Overlays use the map’s 45° orthographic camera projection. Magenta lines are extracted from exported GLB water triangles. Red markers show district centers.</p><table><tr><th>District / water body</th><th>Maximum error</th><th>Reference</th></tr>'''+rows+'</table>'+photos+'<p>Basemap © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL. <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">Attribution and license</a>.</p>')
link=Path('outputs/florida_coastal_atlas/30a-final')
if not link.exists():link.symlink_to(O.resolve(),target_is_directory=True)
print('report and six screenshots exist:', all((O/f'{s}-{w}.png').exists() for s in ['seaside','rosemary','alys'] for w in [390,1440]))
